/playwright-report
/test-results
/.state

# Run scratch that the suite rewrites on every execution, so it must never be a committed artifact.
# Each of these was tracked, and because an ignore rule does not apply to a tracked file the tree went
# dirty after every run and the committed copy was only ever a stale snapshot. They stay on disk.
#
#   /test-data/runtime.json     a data bag one fixture writes for another to read; only this file
#                               lives in test-data/, and it carries no fixture the suite needs to run.
#   /data/data-transfer/*.csv   the files the import specs upload and the export specs overwrite.
#                               Deliberately not `/data/`: data/images/ holds twelve fixture images
#                               the specs attach and those are read-only inputs worth tracking.
#
# `.state/` needs no entry of its own -- `/.state` above already covers it.
/test-data/runtime.json
/data/data-transfer/*.csv
